# Reference Tooltip

:theorem: {:label: thm-x}

  For every graph on $n$ vertices the edge count is at most $n(n-1)/2$, with
  equality exactly for the complete graph.

::

The bound above is the workhorse of the argument. We invoke it now: by
:ref:thm-x:: the dense case is immediate, and the rest of the proof only has to
handle the sparse remainder.
